====================================================================================================
(A) Two programs: which fixed priors reproduce the cn-MAP sets on every sample (n = 1..6)?
====================================================================================================
c = 1/20 (c k = 1/2): 55986 samples
   fixed prior delta_coin (w(f)=0)   : MAP set equal to the cn-MAP set on 54894, different on 1092
   fixed prior uniform (1,1)         : MAP set equal to the cn-MAP set on 55986, different on 0
   fixed prior (1, 2^-20)            : MAP set equal to the cn-MAP set on 54894, different on 1092
c = 1/5 (c k = 2): 55986 samples
   fixed prior delta_coin (w(f)=0)   : MAP set equal to the cn-MAP set on 55986, different on 0
   fixed prior uniform (1,1)         : MAP set equal to the cn-MAP set on 54894, different on 1092
   fixed prior (1, 2^-20)            : MAP set equal to the cn-MAP set on 55986, different on 0
Reading: for c k > 1 the prior delta_coin (no full support) reproduces the cn-MAPs on every sample;
for c k < 1 the full-support prior (1,1) does, consistent with Prop 2.2 (no sample satisfies (a),(b) there).

